<<<
In a large class, of which recriminatory (OEDrikri’minatori)may be taken as the type, there are regularly two pronunciations, one academic as above, & the other with a secondary accent or clearly pronounced 4 (rikri/minatori) used by ordinary people.
===
In a large class, of which *recriminatory* (OED rĭkrĭ'mĭnatorĭ) may be taken as the type, there are regularly two pronunciations, one academic as above, & the other with a secondary accent or clearly pronounced ā (rĭkrĭ'mĭnātorĭ) used by ordinary people.
>>>

<<<
The unsatisfactory clipping of words like voluntar(y)ism & accompan(y)ist (see -1sT) is perhaps due to this dislike of many syllables unrelieved by an accent. The word CONTUMELY, With its five pronunciations, is an interesting case, discussed separately.
===
The unsatisfactory clipping of words like *voluntar(y)ism* & *accompan(y)ist* (see ^^-IST^^) is perhaps due to this dislike of many syllables unrelieved by an accent. The word ^^CONTUMELY^^, with its five pronunciations, is an interesting case, discussed separately.
>>>

